<section class="site-shell card scroll-reveal" aria-labelledby="short-bio-title">
  <h2 id="short-bio-title" class="mono-font">Short Bio</h2>
  <p>
    I received dual B.Eng. degrees (with honors) from <a href="https://www.bupt.edu.cn">Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications</a>, China, and <a href="https://www.qmul.ac.uk/">Queen Mary University of London (QMUL)</a>, U.K., in 2020; an M.Sc. degree (with distinction) from <a href="https://www.imperial.ac.uk/">Imperial College London</a>, U.K., in 2021; and a Ph.D. degree from QMUL in 2024, advised by <a href="https://www.eee.hku.hk/~yuanwei/">Prof. Yuanwei Liu</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    I am currently a Research Assistant Professor at <a href="https://www.hku.hk/">The University of Hong Kong</a>. Prior to that, I was a Postdoctoral Researcher with QMUL from 2024 to 2025. My research focuses on near-field communications, integrated sensing and communications, and optimization theory for next-generation wireless systems. I have received the Best Student Paper Award at IEEE VTC2022-Fall, the 2023 IEEE Daniel E. Noble Fellowship Award, and the 2025 Andrea Goldsmith Young Scholar Award. I was also recognized as an Exemplary Reviewer for IEEE Wireless Communications Letters in 2023 and IEEE Communications Letters in 2024. I serve as an Editor for IEEE Transactions on Communications.
  </p>
</section>

